The '''International dollar''' (symbol: '''$''' or '''I$'''; [[ISO 4217]] code: '''XID''') is the official [[W:Reserve currency|reserve currency]] and primary medium of exchange for the [[Adonian Community]]. It is issued and regulated by the [[Adonian Monetary Authority]] (AMA), an independent institution of the Adonian Community headquartered in [[Areza]]. The International dollar serves as the common currency for international transactions between member states, the official currency for Adonian Community institutions, and one of the world's dominant [[W:Reserve currency|reserve currencies]].

The International dollar was introduced on 15 September 1948, following the [[Treaty of Calatayud]] which established the Adonian Monetary Authority. It replaced a basket of national currencies previously used for international settlements among member states. 

As of 2026, the International dollar is used as the official or de facto currency in X of the 2xx Adonian Community member states (the vast majority being [[W:City-state|city]] or [[W:Microstates|microstates]]), with the remaining members maintaining their national currencies with convertibility for domestic transactions. The currency is also widely used in international trade, particularly in commodities markets, and serves as a benchmark currency for global financial markets.

== History ==
{{Main|History of the International dollar}}

=== Background and creation ===
The concept of a common international currency emerged from the devastation of the [[Great Adonian War]], which had disrupted global trade and financial systems. The [[1947 Adonian Economic Conference]] in [[Calatayud]], [[Andalus]], established the framework for post-war economic cooperation, including the creation of the Adonian Monetary Authority and the International dollar.

The founding members of the Adonian Community sought to create a currency that would:

* Facilitate international trade and financial transactions
* Provide stability in international exchange rates
* Serve as a neutral medium of exchange not dominated by any single nation
* Support the economic reconstruction of war-torn regions

The International dollar was formally established by the [[Treaty of Calatayud (1947)|Calatayud Treaty]], signed on 12 June 1947, and entered into circulation on 15 September 1948. The initial value was set at 0.888671 grams of fine gold (equivalent to $1 at the time), with member states agreeing to maintain their currencies within a 1% band of their established par values.

=== Recent developments ===

== Administration ==
The International dollar is administered by the [[Adonian Monetary Authority]] (AMA), an independent institution of the Adonian Community. The AMA is headquartered in [[Areza]], with regional offices in [[Ampuria]], [[Okami]], [[Mazar]], and [[Castejón]].

=== Governance ===
The AMA is governed by the [[Monetary Council of the Adonian Community|Monetary Council]], consisting of:

* One representative from each member state using the International dollar as legal tender
* The [[Governor of the Adonian Monetary Authority]] (serving as chair)
* The [[Deputy Governors]] (three positions)

Decisions on monetary policy require a two-thirds majority of the Monetary Council, with each member state having one vote regardless of economic size.

=== Monetary policy ===
The AMA's primary monetary policy objective is [[W:Price stability|price stability]], defined as an annual inflation rate of "below, but close to, 2% over the medium term." Secondary objectives include:

* Supporting balanced economic growth
* Maintaining financial stability
* Facilitating international trade and payments

The AMA implements monetary policy through:

* [[Open market operations]]
* [[Interest rate policy]] (the [[Adonian Refinancing Rate]])
* [[Reserve requirements]] for member state central banks
* [[Foreign exchange intervention]]

=== Issuance ===
The AMA has exclusive authority to authorize the issuance of International dollar banknotes and coins. Physical currency is produced by authorized national mints in member states according to AMA specifications. The AMA also issues digital International dollars through the [[Adonian Payments System]].

== Value and exchange rates ==
{{Main|Exchange rates of the International dollar}}
The International dollar has been a floating currency since 1973, with its value determined by [[foreign exchange markets]]. The AMA publishes daily reference exchange rates against major currencies, calculated as a weighted average of transactions in major foreign exchange markets.

=== Exchange rate regime ===
Member states using the International dollar as legal tender are part of the [[International dollar zone]], within which no exchange controls or restrictions apply. Member states maintaining national currencies operate under various exchange rate arrangements:

* '''Currency board arrangements''' (x member states)
* '''Fixed peg to International dollar''' (x member states)
* '''Crawling peg''' (x member states)
* '''Managed float''' (x member states)
* '''Independent float''' (x member states)

=== Reserve currency status ===
The International dollar is one of the world's primary [[Reserve currency|reserve currencies]]. As of Q4 2025, International dollar-denominated assets accounted for approximately 52% of global foreign exchange reserves, compared to 18% for the [[TBA]] and 11% for the [[Meso]].

The International dollar's reserve currency status is supported by:

* The size and depth of International dollar financial markets
* The credibility of AMA monetary policy
* The economic weight of the Adonian Community
* The currency's use in international trade and commodity pricing

== Banknotes and coins ==
{{Main|Banknotes of the International dollar|Coins of the International dollar}}

=== Banknotes ===
International dollar banknotes are issued in seven denominations: $5, $10, $20, $50, $100, $200, and $500. Each denomination features:

* A portrait of a significant figure in world history or culture
* Architectural or natural landmarks
* Advanced security features including [[W:Polymer substrate|polymer substrate]], [[W:Optically variable ink|optically variable ink]], and [[W:Holographic strips|holographic strips]]

