=== Coins ===
International dollar coins are issued in six denominations: 1¢, 5¢, 10¢, 25¢, 50¢, and $1. Coins feature:

* The Adonian Community emblem on the obverse
* Denomination and year on the reverse
* Varying metallic compositions by denomination

== Legal status ==

=== International dollar zone ===
The International dollar zone comprises member states that have adopted the International dollar as their sole legal tender. As of 2026, X member states are part of the International dollar zone:

* [[Areza]]

Member states that have retained their national currencies while participating in the Adonian Community include:

* {{Flag|Balisca}}

=== Legal tender status ===
International dollar banknotes and coins are legal tender in all International dollar zone member states. Creditors are required to accept payment in International dollars for debts denominated in that currency. Member states retaining national currencies may designate the International dollar as either:

* '''Legal tender alongside national currency''' (dual currency regime)
* '''Foreign currency with unrestricted circulation''' (foreign currency regime)

